{
  "about": "Input to scripts/map_library_catalogue.py, which copies its scans (and the ids and checksums of the eight L7014 sheets the project started with) into data/sources/map_library.json; nothing reads this file at run time, and setup downloads no maps. l7014: US Army Map Service L7014 1:50,000 GeoPDFs from the USGS store (georeferenced from their own embedded registration points). scans: older scanned maps. data/scans/<id>.json holds control points in pixels of data/raw/scans/<id>/work.jpg, so work.jpg must be reproduced exactly: it is either the archive's file itself (no 'derive'), or the archive's file is kept as 'source_file' and converted as 'derive' says (jp2_reduce: JPEG 2000 resolution levels to drop, each halving the size; width: Lanczos resize to this width; jpeg_quality: JPEG quality, saved without chroma subsampling). bytes and sha256 describe the archive's file as first downloaded; work_size is [width, height] of work.jpg. page, when given, is a human-readable catalogue page.",
